<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pyatigorsk</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pyatigorsk is a spa town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stavropol">Stavropol</a> Krai, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, in the Caucasian Mineral Waters area at the foot of Mount Beshtau, whose five peaks give the town its name. Founded as a Russian fort and resort in the early 19th century, it is associated with the poet Mikhail Lermontov, who was killed in a duel there in 1841. In 1918 it was a seat of the Soviet governments of the Terek and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-caucasus">North Caucasus</a>.</p></div>
